    "opening": "Food cost percentage compares the cost of food used during a period with food sales from that same period. It is useful for checking waste, portion control and purchasing after the fact. It differs from the recipe cost of one dish, which helps set a menu price before the sale. Mixing those two measures can make a menu seem healthy while inventory is disappearing faster than planned.",
