    "opening": "A restaurant sales forecast starts with the number of orders your location can attract and serve, not last year's revenue multiplied by a growth percentage. Forecast lunch, dinner and delivery separately because their checks and costs differ. Then test the result against seats, table turns, kitchen throughput and staff coverage. A revenue target that needs more orders than a Friday rush can process is not a usable forecast.",
