    "opening": "Starting a restaurant means proving that a specific menu can attract enough local orders at a price that covers food, payroll and occupancy. Define the customer and service model first. Then check the premises and approvals, price the recipes, plan staffing and compare required orders with realistic capacity. Opening cash and monthly operating profit are separate calculations.",
